<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swedish–Norwegian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swedish–Norwegian War was a short war in July and August 1814 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, which had declared independence after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kiel">Treaty of Kiel</a> transferred it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> to Sweden. Swedish forces under Crown Prince Charles John (Bernadotte) quickly gained the upper hand, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/convention-of-moss">Convention of Moss</a> ended the fighting. Norway kept its new constitution but entered a personal union with Sweden that lasted until 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swedish-norwegian-war.jpg" alt="Swedish–Norwegian War" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oscar Wergeland · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eidsvoll_riksraad_1814.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
